  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/35dff03cbdc616b24b81ae428d0f83c925f44493b050c0820fec359b6d05cb73.png)\n\nWhat inequality describes the shaded region shown above?\n\n$y$ \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}",
  "worked_solution": "We need to decide which inequality symbol to use. Since the line is dashed, we will use a strict inequality. Since the shaded region is * below* the line, the inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* those on the line.\n\nSo, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<x-1.\n$$",
